1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:02,053
This tiny dot

2
00:00:02,103 --> 00:00:03,008
is Earth…

3
00:00:03,058 --> 00:00:05,640
seen from six billion

4
00:00:05,690 --> 00:00:07,553
kilometres away.

5
00:00:08,147 --> 00:00:09,263
Everyone you've

6
00:00:09,313 --> 00:00:10,169
ever loved.

7
00:00:10,219 --> 00:00:11,576
Every war.

8
00:00:11,626 --> 00:00:14,024
Every heartbreak.

9
00:00:14,074 --> 00:00:15,527
All of it…

10
00:00:15,577 --> 00:00:17,546
on a speck of dust.

11
00:00:18,006 --> 00:00:19,685
And here we are…

12
00:00:19,735 --> 00:00:20,622
worrying about

13
00:00:20,672 --> 00:00:21,890
a message we sent.

14
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:23,257
A bad day.

15
00:00:23,307 --> 00:00:24,658
Someone who

16
00:00:24,708 --> 00:00:26,216
didn't call back.

17
00:00:26,808 --> 00:00:28,516
From far enough away…

18
00:00:28,566 --> 00:00:30,030
none of it

19
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:31,512
can be seen.

20
00:00:31,975 --> 00:00:33,184
But up close…

21
00:00:33,234 --> 00:00:35,438
one small kindness

22
00:00:35,488 --> 00:00:36,846
can feel bigger

23
00:00:36,896 --> 00:00:38,580
than a galaxy.

24
00:00:39,210 --> 00:00:40,590
Maybe being small

25
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:43,386
makes our problems lighter…

26
00:00:43,436 --> 00:00:44,884
or maybe it makes

27
00:00:44,934 --> 00:00:46,918
every feeling rarer.

28
00:00:49,978 --> 00:00:51,755
So does being small

29
00:00:51,805 --> 00:00:54,283
make us matter less…

30
00:00:54,333 --> 00:00:55,770
or more?

